  "name": "Live extraction \u2014 thousand-separated net mass",
  "why": "RISKS.md N6, FIXED. This read 'Net mass: 24,500.00 kg' as 24.0 \u2014 one regex stopped at the thousand separator, and the shared parser stripped every comma, so the European '24,5' became 245. A thousand-fold error one way and a ten-fold error the other, both silent, because 24 kg of steel is a plausible quantity and no downstream check fires.\n\nparse_quantity now decides which separator is the decimal point: the rightmost one that could be. Kept as a golden case because this is the single most consequential number the engine reads \u2014 mass drives the mark-up, the embedded emissions and the CBAM charge.",
